  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Two touches – look up first",
  "description": "Four v four with a goalkeeper in each team on a small pitch with two 5-a-side goals. Each player may touch the ball at most twice (three times for younger or less experienced players). A goal only counts if the ball is rolled or passed in from about ten metres or closer – so the team has to play its way forward instead of shooting from distance.\n\nPlay in spells of three to four minutes. Variation: one touch only, but the player who wins the ball from the other team may touch it freely. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up before the ball arrives – know where it is going before you receive it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep moving so that the player on the ball always has someone to pass to."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Stand where there is an open passing lane, not behind an opponent."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Your first touch should set the ball up for the next pass."
    }
  ],
